\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When my love to Christ grows weak,
\par When for deeper faith I seek,
\par Then in thought I go to thee,
\par Garden of Gethsemane!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There I walk amid the shades,
\par While the lingering twillight fades,
\par See that suffering, friendless One,
\par Weeping, praying there alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When my love for man grows weak,
\par When for stronger faith I seek,
\par Hill of Calvary! I go
\par To Thy scenes to fear and woe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There behold His agony,
\par Suffered on the bitter Tree;
\par See His anguish, see His faith,
\par Love triumphant still in death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then to life I turn again,
\par Learning all the worth of pain,
\par Learning all the might that lies
\par In a full self-sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And I praise with firmer faith
\par Christ who vanquished pain and death;
\par And to Christ enthroned above
\par Raise my song of selfless love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

